@0    = ~Uh, <CHARNAME>. As much as I hate to use the word "cosy" in relation to him, you and Edwin seem to be it lately.~
@1    = ~Silence! I have been no such thing, I assure you. It is your own tiny, sensuality-obsessed brain that has constructed this absurdity.~
@2    = ~If you don't mind, I was having a chat with <CHARNAME>, Edwin. You got something to say?~
@3    = ~I would laugh if this was not so painfully tragic. You loutish thug, attempting to court my <CHARNAME>? Ridiculous! (Did I...just say "my"? Quick - nobody noticed...)~
@4    = ~Faren, I think of you as a friend, but nothing more.~
@5    = ~Back off, Faren. I like Edwin's company more than yours.~
@6    = ~Edwin, I think you've got the wrong idea. I have something going with Faren.~
@7    = ~Whatever. You want this megalomaniac wizard, I won't stop you.~
@8    = ~I see. You wish for us to be 'friends'. You go off with your ale-swilling ape. See if I care. (Don't let her see, please don't let her see...)~
